# @lace-cloud/* packages live in GitHub Packages (public, but the npm
# endpoint still requires auth — a GitHub quirk). Any GitHub token with
# `read:packages` works; in CI, GITHUB_TOKEN does so by default. Local
# contributors set NODE_AUTH_TOKEN to a personal classic PAT with
# `read:packages` (see README "Local development" section).
@lace-cloud:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${NODE_AUTH_TOKEN}
